-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992, 1992 c. 4 -- part ssc5.
-- PART VI, MISCELLANEOUS PROVISIONS RELATING TO PARTS I TO V (ss 112 to 122).  Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from legislation.gov.uk (point in time
-- 2026-07-08); it is not the official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".
-- Reading a result: JUST FALSE is the Act saying no in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (NOTES.md).
-- K3 (s 174, line 4342): in this file "the Administration Act" is the Social Security Administration Act 1992, "the 1975 Act" is the Social Security Act 1975 and "the 1986 Act" is the Social Security Act 1986.
-- Every NOT is bracketed.  Most of ss 112 to 121 are powers to make regulations: they are not encoded as
-- rules (coverage reason 2, machinery), except where the section states its own limit or default.
-- Section 122(1) is the Act's list of defined terms.  Each term is one record of how the Act defines it
-- (`s 122(1) A definition`), in text order, with the few that compute something written as functions.
-- "the upper accrual point" is the core's constant and is not defined again here.

§ `Part VI -- Miscellaneous provisions relating to Parts I to V (ss 112-122)`

§§ `s 112 -- certain sums to be earnings`

-- The sums mentioned in subsection (3).
-- src:2454 | (3) The sums referred to in subsection (2) above are the following—
-- src:2455 | (a) a sum payable in respect of arrears of pay in pursuance of an order for reinstatement or re-engagement under the Employment Rights Act 1996;
-- src:2456 | (b) a sum payable by way of pay in pursuance of an order under that Act or the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 for the continuation of a contract of employment;
-- src:2457 | (c) a sum payable by way of remuneration in pursuance of a protective award under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992.
@ref s 112(3) (src:2454-2457)
DECLARE `s 112(3) Sum` IS ONE OF
    `s 112(3)(a) a sum payable in respect of arrears of pay in pursuance of an order for reinstatement or re-engagement under the Employment Rights Act 1996`
    `s 112(3)(b) a sum payable by way of pay in pursuance of an order under that Act or the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 for the continuation of a contract of employment`
    `s 112(3)(c) a sum payable by way of remuneration in pursuance of a protective award under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992`
    `s 112(3) some other sum`

GIVEN sum IS A `s 112(3) Sum`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112(3) the sum is one the subsection mentions` MEANS
    CONSIDER sum
    WHEN `s 112(3)(a) a sum payable in respect of arrears of pay in pursuance of an order for reinstatement or re-engagement under the Employment Rights Act 1996` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 112(3)(b) a sum payable by way of pay in pursuance of an order under that Act or the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 for the continuation of a contract of employment` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 112(3)(c) a sum payable by way of remuneration in pursuance of a protective award under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 112(3) some other sum` THEN FALSE

-- "employment protection entitlement" means a mentioned sum or a prescribed part of one, and prescribed amounts
-- which regulations provide are to be treated as related to any of those sums.
-- src:2450 | (2) In subsection (1) above “employment protection entitlement” means—
-- src:2451 | (a) any sum, or a prescribed part of any sum, mentioned in subsection (3) below; and
-- src:2452 | (b) prescribed amounts which the regulations provide are to be treated as related to any of those sums.
@ref s 112(2) (src:2450-2452)
GIVEN sum IS A `s 112(3) Sum`
      `only a part of that sum is in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that part is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is prescribed and the regulations provide it is to be treated as related to one of the mentioned sums` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112(2) the sum is an employment protection entitlement` MEANS
    IF     (`s 112(3) the sum is one the subsection mentions` sum AND ((NOT `only a part of that sum is in question`) OR `that part is prescribed`))
        OR `the amount is prescribed and the regulations provide it is to be treated as related to one of the mentioned sums`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“employment protection entitlement” means"

§§ `s 113 -- disqualification and suspension`

-- Except where regulations otherwise provide, a person is disqualified for receiving a benefit under Parts II to V,
-- and an increase is not payable for his wife, husband or civil partner, for any period of absence from Great
-- Britain or of imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
-- src:2460 | (1) Except where regulations otherwise provide, a person shall be disqualified for receiving any benefit under Parts II to V of this Act, and an increase of such benefit shall not be payable in respect of any person as the beneficiary’s wife, husband or civil partner, for any period during which the person—
-- src:2461 | (a) is absent from Great Britain; or
-- src:2462 | (b) is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
@ref s 113(1) (src:2460-2462)
GIVEN `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is absent from Great Britain for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(1) the person is disqualified for receiving the benefit for the period` MEANS
    IF `regulations otherwise provide`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where regulations otherwise provide"
    ELSE
        IF `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of this Act` AND (`the person is absent from Great Britain for the period` OR `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period`)
        THEN JUST TRUE   -- the text says so in its own words: "a person shall be disqualified for receiving any benefit under Parts II to V"
        ELSE NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any period during which the person (a) is absent from Great Britain; or (b) is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody"

-- src:2460 | (1) Except where regulations otherwise provide, a person shall be disqualified for receiving any benefit under Parts II to V of this Act, and an increase of such benefit shall not be payable in respect of any person as the beneficiary’s wife, husband or civil partner, for any period during which the person—
-- src:2461 | (a) is absent from Great Britain; or
-- src:2462 | (b) is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody.
@ref s 113(1) (src:2460-2462)
GIVEN `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is absent from Great Britain for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113(1) an increase of the benefit is payable in respect of the person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner for the period` MEANS
    IF `regulations otherwise provide`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Except where regulations otherwise provide"
    ELSE
        IF `the benefit is a benefit under Parts II to V of this Act` AND (`the person is absent from Great Britain for the period` OR `the person is undergoing imprisonment or detention in legal custody for the period`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an increase of such benefit shall not be payable in respect of any person as the beneficiary's wife, husband or civil partner"
        ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is not triggered

§§ `ss 115 and 116 -- Crown employment and Her Majesty's forces`

-- src:2481 | (1) Subject to the provisions of this section, Parts I to V and this Part of this Act apply to persons employed by or under the Crown in like manner as if they were employed by a private person.
-- src:2482 | (2) Subsection (1) above does not apply to persons serving as members of Her Majesty’s forces in their capacity as such.
@ref s 115(1) (src:2481-2482)
GIVEN `the person is employed by or under the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(1) Parts I to V and this Part apply to the person as if employed by a private person` MEANS
    IF `the person is serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces in that capacity`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 115(2) "Subsection (1) above does not apply to persons serving as members of Her Majesty's forces in their capacity as such"
    ELSE
        IF `the person is employed by or under the Crown`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "persons employed by or under the Crown"

-- src:2483 | (3) Employment as a member of Her Majesty’s forces and any other prescribed employment under the Crown are not, and are not to be treated as, employed earner’s employment for any of the purposes of Part V of this Act.
@ref s 115(3) (src:2483)
GIVEN `the employment is as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is other prescribed employment under the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 115(3) the employment is employed earner's employment for the purposes of Part V` MEANS
    IF `the employment is as a member of Her Majesty's forces` OR `the employment is other prescribed employment under the Crown`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are not, and are not to be treated as, employed earner's employment for any of the purposes of Part V of this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of those two employments

DECLARE `s 116(1) Purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Parts I to IV of this Act`
    `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Part V of this Act`
    `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of this Part of this Act`
    `s 116(1)(b) a purpose of a provision of the Administration Act in its application to him as an employed earner`
    `s 116(1) some other purpose`

-- Subject to s 115(2) and (3): a member of the forces, while serving, is treated as an employed earner in
-- respect of his membership for the purposes listed.  Section 115(3) takes Part V out of it.
-- src:2486 | (1) Subject to section 115(2) and (3) above and to this section, a person who is serving as a member of Her Majesty’s forces shall, while he is so serving, be treated as an employed earner, in respect of his membership of those forces, for the purposes—
-- src:2487 | (a) of Parts I to V and this Part of this Act; and
-- src:2488 | (b) of any provision of the Administration Act in its application to him as an employed earner.
@ref s 116(1) (src:2486-2488)
GIVEN `the person is serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 116(1) Purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(1) the person is treated as an employed earner in respect of membership of the forces` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is serving as a member of Her Majesty's forces shall, while he is so serving"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER purpose
        WHEN `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Parts I to IV of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of Part V of this Act` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 115(3), to which this subsection is "subject": employment as a member of Her Majesty's forces is not employed earner's employment for any purpose of Part V
        WHEN `s 116(1)(a) a purpose of this Part of this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 116(1)(b) a purpose of a provision of the Administration Act in its application to him as an employed earner` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 116(1) some other purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection lists the purposes

-- (3): the forces consist of the establishments and organisations prescribed, in which persons serve under the
-- control of the Defence Council.
-- src:2492 | (3) For the purposes of Parts I to V and this Part of this Act, Her Majesty’s forces shall be taken to consist of such establishments and organisations as may be prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury with the concurrence of the Secretary of State, being establishments and organisations in which persons serve under the control of the Defence Council.
@ref s 116(3) (src:2492)
GIVEN `the establishment or organisation is prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury with the concurrence of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `persons serve in it under the control of the Defence Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 116(3) the establishment or organisation is part of Her Majesty's forces` MEANS
    IF NOT `the establishment or organisation is prescribed by regulations made by the Treasury with the concurrence of the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be taken to consist of such establishments and organisations as may be prescribed"
    ELSE
        IF `persons serve in it under the control of the Defence Council`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text limits what may be prescribed to ones "in which persons serve under the control of the Defence Council" and does not say what follows if regulations go beyond that

§§ `ss 117, 119 and 120 -- regulations that bring in accidents outside Great Britain`

-- The three answers section 94(5) asks for (seam S20): "Subject to sections 117, 119 and 120 below, industrial
-- injuries benefit shall not be payable in respect of an accident happening while the earner is outside Great
-- Britain".  Each exception exists only as far as regulations under that section provide it.
-- src:2494 | (1) The Treasury may with the concurrence of the Secretary of State make regulations modifying provisions of Parts I to V and this Part of this Act and Part II of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999, and any provisions of Chapter II of Part I of the Social Security Act 1998 which correspond to provisions of Part III of the 1975 Act, in such manner as the Treasury think proper, in their application to persons who are or have been, or are to be, employed on board any ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft.
@ref s 117(1) (src:2494)
GIVEN `the earner is or has been, or is to be, employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations under section 117(1) apply the provision to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 117 the accident falls within the exception` MEANS
    IF `the earner is or has been, or is to be, employed on board a ship, vessel, hovercraft or aircraft` AND `regulations under section 117(1) apply the provision to the accident`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exception exists only as regulations under section 117 provide

-- src:2508 | The Treasury may with the concurrence of the Secretary of State make regulations modifying Parts I to V of this Act and Part II of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999, and any provisions of Chapter II of Part I of the Social Security Act 1998 which correspond to provisions of Part III of the 1975 Act, in such manner as the Treasury think proper, in their application to persons who are or have been outside Great Britain at any prescribed time or in any prescribed circumstances.
@ref s 119 (src:2508)
GIVEN `the earner is or has been outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations under section 119 apply the provision to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 119 the accident falls within the exception` MEANS
    IF `the earner is or has been outside Great Britain at a prescribed time or in prescribed circumstances` AND `regulations under section 119 apply the provision to the accident`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exception exists only as regulations under section 119 provide

-- (2) "Continental shelf operations" (seam S25): activities which, with paragraphs (a) and (d) of section 11(8)
-- of the Petroleum Act 1998 omitted, would nevertheless fall within section 11(2) of that Act.
-- src:2511 | (2) “Continental shelf operations” means any activities which, if paragraphs (a) and (d) of subsection (8) of section 11 of the Petroleum Act 1998 (application of civil law to certain offshore activities) were omitted, would nevertheless fall within subsection (2) of that section.
@ref s 120(2) (src:2511)
GIVEN `the employment is in connection with activities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the activities would fall within section 11(2) of the Petroleum Act 1998 if paragraphs (a) and (d) of subsection (8) of that section were omitted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` MEANS
    `the employment is in connection with activities` AND `the activities would fall within section 11(2) of the Petroleum Act 1998 if paragraphs (a) and (d) of subsection (8) of that section were omitted`

-- src:2510 | (1) The Treasury may with the concurrence of the Secretary of State make regulations modifying Parts I to V and this Part of this Act and Part II of the Social Security Contributions (Transfer of Functions, etc.) Act 1999, and any provisions of Chapter II of Part I of the Social Security Act 1998 which correspond to provisions of Part III of the 1975 Act, in such manner as the Treasury think proper, in their application to persons (“continental shelf workers”) in any prescribed employment (whether under a contract of service or not) in connection with continental shelf operations.
@ref s 120(1) (src:2510)
GIVEN `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employment is prescribed employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `regulations under section 120(1) apply the provision to the accident` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 120 the accident falls within the exception` MEANS
    IF `s 120(2) the employment is in connection with continental shelf operations` AND `the employment is prescribed employment` AND `regulations under section 120(1) apply the provision to the accident`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the exception exists only as regulations under section 120 provide

§§ `s 122(1) -- the Act's defined terms`

-- "In Parts I to V above and this Part of this Act, unless the context otherwise requires": a defined meaning
-- applies unless the context otherwise requires.  Whether it does is a judgment, taken as a plain input.
-- src:2532 | (1) In Parts I to V above and this Part of this Act, unless the context otherwise requires—
@ref s 122(1) (src:2532)
GIVEN `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(1) the defined meaning applies` MEANS
    IF `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In Parts I to V above and this Part of this Act, unless the context otherwise requires" -- the context otherwise requires, so the defined meaning does not apply
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 122(1) Kind of pension for deferment` IS ONE OF
    `s 122(1) a Category A or Category B retirement pension`
    `s 122(1) a shared additional pension`
    `s 122(1) some other pension`

-- "deferred" is read as sections 55(3) and 55C(3) read it (seam S37: those sections answer).
-- src:2558 | “deferred” and “period of deferment”—
-- src:2559 | in relation to a Category A or Category B retirement pension, have the meanings given by section 55(3), and
-- src:2560 | in relation to a shared additional pension, have the meanings given by section 55C(3);
@ref s 122(1) “deferred” (src:2558-2560)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 122(1) Kind of pension for deferment`
      `s 55(3) the pension is deferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122(1) the pension is deferred` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 122(1) a Category A or Category B retirement pension` THEN `s 55(3) the pension is deferred`
    WHEN `s 122(1) a shared additional pension` THEN `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred`
    WHEN `s 122(1) some other pension` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a Category A or Category B retirement pension" and "in relation to a shared additional pension"

-- "tax year": the 12 months beginning with 6 April.  A year is named by the calendar year in which it begins.
-- src:2619 | “tax year” means the 12 months beginning with 6th April in any year, the expression “1978-79” meaning the tax year beginning with 6th April 1978, and any correspondingly framed reference to a pair of successive years being construed as a reference to the tax year beginning with 6th April in the earlier of them;
@ref s 122(1) “tax year” (src:2619)
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Tax year`
`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` MEANS
    `Tax year` WITH
        `calendar year in which it begins` IS
            IF date AT LEAST (Date 6 4 (DATE_YEAR date)) THEN DATE_YEAR date ELSE (DATE_YEAR date) MINUS 1

-- "1978-79" means the tax year beginning with 6 April 1978: a correspondingly framed reference to a pair of
-- successive years is the tax year beginning with 6 April in the earlier of them.
-- src:2619 | “tax year” means the 12 months beginning with 6th April in any year, the expression “1978-79” meaning the tax year beginning with 6th April 1978, and any correspondingly framed reference to a pair of successive years being construed as a reference to the tax year beginning with 6th April in the earlier of them;
@ref s 122(1) “tax year” (src:2619)
GIVEN `the earlier year` IS A NUMBER
      `the later year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `Tax year`
`s 122(1) the tax year named by a pair of successive years` MEANS
    IF `the later year` EQUALS `the earlier year` PLUS 1
    THEN JUST (`Tax year` WITH `calendar year in which it begins` IS `the earlier year`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a pair of successive years"

-- "tax week": one of the successive periods in a tax year beginning with its first day and every seventh day
-- after; the last day (or in a tax year ending in a leap year the last two days) is a separate tax week.
-- Counting from 0 at 6 April, offset DIV 7 plus 1 gives 1 to 52, and the 365th and 366th days (offsets 364, 365) both give 53.
-- src:2618 | “tax week” means one of the successive periods in a tax year beginning with the first day of that year and every seventh day thereafter, the last day of a tax year (or, in the case of a tax year ending in a leap year, the last two days) to be treated accordingly as a separate tax week;
@ref s 122(1) “tax week” (src:2618)
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Tax week`
`s 122(1) the tax week containing the date` MEANS
    `Tax week` WITH
        `the tax year` IS `s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` date
        `number of the week in the year` IS (FLOOR (((Day date) MINUS (Day firstDay)) DIVIDED BY 7)) PLUS 1
    WHERE
        firstDay MEANS Date 6 4 ((`s 122(1) the tax year containing the date` date)'s `calendar year in which it begins`)

-- "week": a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday (the core's Week convention names this meaning).
-- src:2624 | “week” ... means a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday;
@ref s 122(1) “week” (src:2624)
GIVEN date IS A DATE
GIVETH A Period
`s 122(1) the week containing the date` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `the first day` IS date MINUS ((Day date) MODULO 7)
        `the last day`  IS (date MINUS ((Day date) MODULO 7)) PLUS 6

-- "qualifying earnings factor": the lower earnings limit for the tax year in question multiplied by 52.
-- src:2604 | “qualifying earnings factor” means an earnings factor equal to the lower earnings limit for the tax year in question multiplied by 52;
@ref s 122(1) “qualifying earnings factor” (src:2604)
GIVEN limits IS A `Earnings limits`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 122(1) the qualifying earnings factor in pounds` MEANS
    limits's `lower earnings limit` TIMES 52

-- The rest of the terms, in text order.  Each is one record of how the Act defines the term.
-- src:2533 | “additional Class 4 percentage” is to be construed in accordance with section 15(3ZA)(b) above;
@ref s 122(1) “additional Class 4 percentage” (src:2533)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 122(1) additional Class 4 percentage` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
        `what it points at or says` IS "section 15(3ZA)(b) above"

-- src:2534 | “additional primary percentage” is to be construed in accordance with section 8(2)(b) above;
@ref s 122(1) “additional primary percentage” (src:2534)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 122(1) additional primary percentage` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
        `what it points at or says` IS "section 8(2)(b) above"

-- src:2535 | “adult disability payment” means disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022;
@ref s 122(1) “adult disability payment” (src:2535)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 122(1) adult disability payment` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "disability assistance given in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022"

-- src:2536 | “age-related secondary percentage” is to be construed in accordance with section 9A(2) above;
@ref s 122(1) “age-related secondary percentage” (src:2536)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 122(1) age-related secondary percentage` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a construction by reference to another provision`
        `what it points at or says` IS "section 9A(2) above"

-- src:2537 | “Bank of England base rate” means—
-- src:2538 | the rate announced from time to time by the Monetary Policy Committee of the Bank of England as the official dealing rate, being the rate at which the Bank is willing to enter into transactions for providing short term liquidity in the money markets, or
-- src:2539 | where an order under section 19 of the Bank of England Act 1998 is in force, any equivalent rate determined by the Treasury under that section;
@ref s 122(1) “Bank of England base rate” (src:2537-2539)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 122(1) Bank of England base rate` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "the rate announced from time to time by the Monetary Policy Committee of the Bank of England as the official dealing rate, or, where an order under section 19 of the Bank of England Act 1998 is in force, any equivalent rate determined by the Treasury under that section"

-- src:2540 | “beneficiary”, in relation to any benefit, means the person entitled to that benefit;
@ref s 122(1) “beneficiary” (src:2540)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 122(1) beneficiary` MEANS
    `s 122(1) A definition` WITH
        `the way it is defined` IS `s 122(1) a definition by "means"`
        `what it points at or says` IS "the person entitled to that benefit"

-- src:2541 | “benefit” means—
-- src:2542 | benefit under Parts II to V of this Act other than Old Cases payments;
-- src:2543 | as respects any period before 1st July 1992 but not before 6th April 1975, benefit under Part II of the 1975 Act; or
-- src:2544 | as respects any period before 6th April 1975, benefit under—
-- src:2545 | the National Insurance Act 1946 or 1965; or
-- src:2546 | the National Insurance (Industrial Injuries) Act 1946 or 1965;
-- src:2547 | (For the meaning of “benefit” in Part 1, see also section 19B)
@ref s 122(1) “benefit” (src:2541-2547)
GIVETH A `s 122(1) A definition`
`s 122(1) benefit` MEANS
